---A single advertiser in Display & Video 360 (DV360).
---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.Advertiser
---@field adServerConfig? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserAdServerConfig Required. Immutable. Ad server related settings of the advertiser.
---@field entityStatus? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserEntityStatusEnum Required. Controls whether or not insertion orders and line items of the advertiser can spend their budgets and bid on inventory. * Accepted values are `ENTITY_STATUS_ACTIVE`, `ENTITY_STATUS_PAUSED` and `ENTITY_STATUS_SCHEDULED_FOR_DELETION`. * If set to `ENTITY_STATUS_SCHEDULED_FOR_DELETION`, the advertiser will be deleted 30 days from when it was first scheduled for deletion.
---@field servingConfig? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserTargetingConfig Targeting settings related to ad serving of the advertiser.
---@field partnerId? string Required. Immutable. The unique ID of the partner that the advertiser belongs to.
---@field dataAccessConfig? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserDataAccessConfig Settings that control how advertiser data may be accessed.
---@field defaultLogoAssetId? string Optional. The asset ID of the default logo image for the advertiser. This is the asset ID that will be used by YouTube and Demand ads under this advertiser if a logo asset is not provided. You must use advertisers.adAssets.upload to upload this asset using the API.
---@field integrationDetails? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.IntegrationDetails Integration details of the advertiser. Only integrationCode is currently applicable to advertiser. Other fields of IntegrationDetails are not supported and will be ignored if provided.
---@field defaultBusinessName? string Optional. The default business name for the advertiser. This is the value used by YouTube and Demand Gen ads under this advertiser if a business name is not provided.
---@field containsEuPoliticalAds? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserContainsEuPoliticalAdsEnum Optional. Whether this advertiser contains line items that serve European Union political ads. If this field is set to `DOES_NOT_CONTAIN_EU_POLITICAL_ADVERTISING`, then the following will happen: * Any new line items created under this advertiser will be assigned `DOES_NOT_CONTAIN_EU_POLITICAL_ADVERTISING` if not otherwise specified. * Any existing line items under this advertiser that do not have a set value be updated to `DOES_NOT_CONTAIN_EU_POLITICAL_ADVERTISING` within a day.
---@field prismaEnabled? boolean Whether integration with Mediaocean (Prisma) is enabled. By enabling this, you agree to the following: On behalf of my company, I authorize Mediaocean (Prisma) to send budget segment plans to Google, and I authorize Google to send corresponding reporting and invoices from DV360 to Mediaocean for the purposes of budget planning, billing, and reconciliation for this advertiser.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the advertiser was last updated. Assigned by the system.
---@field generalConfig? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserGeneralConfig Required. General settings of the advertiser.
---@field creativeConfig? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserCreativeConfig Required. Creative related settings of the advertiser.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the advertiser.
---@field billingConfig? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserBillingConfig Required. Billing related settings of the advertiser.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the advertiser. Must be UTF-8 encoded with a maximum size of 240 bytes.
---@field advertiserId? string Output only. The unique ID of the advertiser. Assigned by the system.

---Ad server related settings of an advertiser.
---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserAdServerConfig
---@field cmHybridConfig? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CmHybridConfig The configuration for advertisers that use both Campaign Manager 360 (CM360) and third-party ad servers.
---@field thirdPartyOnlyConfig? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.ThirdPartyOnlyConfig The configuration for advertisers that use third-party ad servers only.

---Billing related settings of an advertiser.
---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserBillingConfig
---@field billingProfileId? string Required. The ID of a billing profile assigned to the advertiser.

---@alias gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserContainsEuPoliticalAdsEnum "EU_POLITICAL_ADVERTISING_STATUS_UNKNOWN"|"CONTAINS_EU_POLITICAL_ADVERTISING"|"DOES_NOT_CONTAIN_EU_POLITICAL_ADVERTISING"

---Creatives related settings of an advertiser.
---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserCreativeConfig
---@field obaComplianceDisabled? boolean Whether or not to disable Google's About this Ad feature that adds badging (to identify the content as an ad) and transparency information (on interaction with About this Ad) to your ads for Online Behavioral Advertising (OBA) and regulatory requirements. About this Ad gives users greater control over the ads they see and helps you explain why they're seeing your ad. [Learn more](//support.google.com/displayvideo/answer/14315795). If you choose to set this field to `true`, note that ads served through Display & Video 360 must comply to the following: * Be Online Behavioral Advertising (OBA) compliant, as per your contract with Google Marketing Platform. * In the European Economic Area (EEA), include transparency information and a mechanism for users to report illegal content in ads. If using an alternative ad badging, transparency, and reporting solution, you must ensure it includes the required transparency information and illegal content flagging mechanism and that you notify Google of any illegal content reports using the appropriate [form](//support.google.com/legal/troubleshooter/1114905?sjid=6787484030557261960-EU#ts=2981967%2C2982031%2C12980091).
---@field dynamicCreativeEnabled? boolean Whether or not the advertiser is enabled for dynamic creatives.
---@field iasClientId? string An ID for configuring campaign monitoring provided by Integral Ad Service (IAS). The DV360 system will append an IAS "Campaign Monitor" tag containing this ID to the creative tag.
---@field videoCreativeDataSharingAuthorized? boolean By setting this field to `true`, you, on behalf of your company, authorize Google to use video creatives associated with this Display & Video 360 advertiser to provide reporting and features related to the advertiser's television campaigns. Applicable only when the advertiser has a CM360 hybrid ad server configuration.

---Settings that control how advertiser related data may be accessed.
---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserDataAccessConfig
---@field sdfConfig? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserSdfConfig Structured Data Files (SDF) settings for the advertiser. If not specified, the SDF settings of the parent partner are used.

---@alias gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserEntityStatusEnum "ENTITY_STATUS_UNSPECIFIED"|"ENTITY_STATUS_ACTIVE"|"ENTITY_STATUS_ARCHIVED"|"ENTITY_STATUS_DRAFT"|"ENTITY_STATUS_PAUSED"|"ENTITY_STATUS_SCHEDULED_FOR_DELETION"

---General settings of an advertiser.
---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserGeneralConfig
---@field currencyCode? string Required. Immutable. Advertiser's currency in ISO 4217 format. Accepted codes and the currencies they represent are: Currency Code : Currency Name * `ARS` : Argentine Peso * `AUD` : Australian Dollar * `BRL` : Brazilian Real * `CAD` : Canadian Dollar * `CHF` : Swiss Franc * `CLP` : Chilean Peso * `CNY` : Chinese Yuan * `COP` : Colombian Peso * `CZK` : Czech Koruna * `DKK` : Danish Krone * `EGP` : Egyption Pound * `EUR` : Euro * `GBP` : British Pound * `HKD` : Hong Kong Dollar * `HUF` : Hungarian Forint * `IDR` : Indonesian Rupiah * `ILS` : Israeli Shekel * `INR` : Indian Rupee * `JPY` : Japanese Yen * `KRW` : South Korean Won * `MXN` : Mexican Pesos * `MYR` : Malaysian Ringgit * `NGN` : Nigerian Naira * `NOK` : Norwegian Krone * `NZD` : New Zealand Dollar * `PEN` : Peruvian Nuevo Sol * `PLN` : Polish Zloty * `RON` : New Romanian Leu * `RUB` : Russian Ruble * `SEK` : Swedish Krona * `TRY` : Turkish Lira * `TWD` : New Taiwan Dollar * `USD` : US Dollar * `ZAR` : South African Rand
---@field domainUrl? string Required. The domain URL of the advertiser's primary website. The system will send this information to publishers that require website URL to associate a campaign with an advertiser. Provide a URL with no path or query string, beginning with `http:` or `https:`. For example, http://www.example.com
---@field timeZone? string Output only. The standard TZ database name of the advertiser's time zone. For example, `America/New_York`. See more at: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_tz_database_time_zones For CM360 hybrid advertisers, the time zone is the same as that of the associated CM360 account; for third-party only advertisers, the time zone is the same as that of the parent partner.

---@alias gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserList gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.Advertiser[]

---Structured Data Files (SDF) settings of an advertiser.
---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserSdfConfig
---@field overridePartnerSdfConfig? boolean Whether or not this advertiser overrides the SDF configuration of its parent partner. By default, an advertiser inherits the SDF configuration from the parent partner. To override the partner configuration, set this field to `true` and provide the new configuration in sdfConfig.
---@field sdfConfig? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.SdfConfig The SDF configuration for the advertiser. * Required when overridePartnerSdfConfig is `true`. * Output only when overridePartnerSdfConfig is `false`.

---Targeting settings related to ad serving of an advertiser.
---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.AdvertiserTargetingConfig
---@field exemptTvFromViewabilityTargeting? boolean Whether or not connected TV devices are exempt from viewability targeting for all video line items under the advertiser.

