---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CreateCustomBiddingAlgorithmsRequest
---@field customBiddingAlgorithmType? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CustomBiddingAlgorithmCustomBiddingAlgorithmTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. The type of custom bidding algorithm.
---@field entityStatus? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CustomBiddingAlgorithmEntityStatusEnum|string Controls whether or not the custom bidding algorithm can be used as a bidding strategy. Accepted values are: * `ENTITY_STATUS_ACTIVE` * `ENTITY_STATUS_ARCHIVED`
---@field sharedAdvertiserIds? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.StringList The IDs of the advertisers who have access to this algorithm. If advertiser_id is set, this field will only consist of that value. This field will not be set if the algorithm [`owner`](/display-video/api/reference/rest/v1/customBiddingAlgorithms#CustomBiddingAlgorithm.FIELDS.oneof_owner) is a partner and is being retrieved using an advertiser [`accessor`](/display-video/api/reference/rest/v1/customBiddingAlgorithms/list#body.QUERY_PARAMETERS.oneof_accessor).
---@field thirdPartyOptimizationPartner? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CustomBiddingAlgorithmThirdPartyOptimizationPartnerEnum|string Optional. Immutable. Designates the third party optimization partner that manages this algorithm.
---@field customBiddingAlgorithmId? string Output only. The unique ID of the custom bidding algorithm. Assigned by the system.
---@field partnerId? string Immutable. The unique ID of the partner that owns the custom bidding algorithm.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the custom bidding algorithm.
---@field advertiserId? string Immutable. The unique ID of the advertiser that owns the custom bidding algorithm.
---@field modelDetails? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CustomBiddingModelDetailsList Output only. The details of custom bidding models for each advertiser who has access. This field may only include the details of the queried advertiser if the algorithm [`owner`](/display-video/api/reference/rest/v1/customBiddingAlgorithms#CustomBiddingAlgorithm.FIELDS.oneof_owner) is a partner and is being retrieved using an advertiser [`accessor`](/display-video/api/reference/rest/v1/customBiddingAlgorithms/list#body.QUERY_PARAMETERS.oneof_accessor).
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the custom bidding algorithm. Must be UTF-8 encoded with a maximum size of 240 bytes.

---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CreateCustomBiddingAlgorithmsRulesRequest
---@field error? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CustomBiddingAlgorithmRulesError Output only. Error code of the rejected rules resource. This field will only be populated when the state is `REJECTED`.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the rules resource.
---@field active? boolean Output only. Whether the rules resource is currently being used for scoring by the parent algorithm.
---@field customBiddingAlgorithmRulesId? string Output only. The unique ID of the rules resource.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time when the rules resource was created.
---@field rules? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CustomBiddingAlgorithmRulesRef Required. Immutable. The reference to the uploaded AlgorithmRules file.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CustomBiddingAlgorithmRulesStateEnum|string Output only. The state of the rules resource.
---@field customBiddingAlgorithmId string Required. The ID of the custom bidding algorithm that owns the rules resource.
---@field partnerId? string The ID of the partner that owns the parent custom bidding algorithm. Only this partner will have write access to this rules resource.
---@field advertiserId? string The ID of the advertiser that owns the parent custom bidding algorithm.

---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CreateCustomBiddingAlgorithmsScriptsRequest
---@field state? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CustomBiddingScriptStateEnum|string Output only. The state of the custom bidding script.
---@field errors? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.ScriptErrorList Output only. Error details of a rejected custom bidding script. This field will only be populated when state is REJECTED.
---@field customBiddingScriptId? string Output only. The unique ID of the custom bidding script.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the custom bidding script.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time when the script was created.
---@field script? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CustomBiddingScriptRef The reference to the uploaded script file.
---@field active? boolean Output only. Whether the script is currently being used for scoring by the parent algorithm.
---@field customBiddingAlgorithmId string Required. The ID of the custom bidding algorithm that owns the script.
---@field advertiserId? string The ID of the advertiser that owns the parent custom bidding algorithm.
---@field partnerId? string The ID of the partner that owns the parent custom bidding algorithm. Only this partner will have write access to this custom bidding script.

---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CreateFirstPartyAndPartnerAudiencesRequest
---@field audienceSource? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.FirstPartyAndPartnerAudienceAudienceSourceEnum|string Output only. The source of the audience.
---@field youtubeAudienceSize? string Output only. The estimated audience size for YouTube network. If the size is less than 1000, the number will be hidden and 0 will be returned due to privacy reasons. Otherwise, the number will be rounded off to two significant digits. Only applicable to first party audiences. Only returned in GET request.
---@field displayMobileWebAudienceSize? string Output only. The estimated mobile web audience size in Display network. If the size is less than 1000, the number will be hidden and 0 will be returned due to privacy reasons. Otherwise, the number will be rounded off to two significant digits. Only applicable to first party audiences. Only returned in GET request.
---@field displayDesktopAudienceSize? string Output only. The estimated desktop audience size in Display network. If the size is less than 1000, the number will be hidden and 0 will be returned due to privacy reasons. Otherwise, the number will be rounded off to two significant digits. Only applicable to first party audiences. Only returned in GET request.
---@field displayAudienceSize? string Output only. The estimated audience size for the Display network. If the size is less than 1000, the number will be hidden and 0 will be returned due to privacy reasons. Otherwise, the number will be rounded off to two significant digits. Only returned in GET request.
---@field displayMobileAppAudienceSize? string Output only. The estimated mobile app audience size in Display network. If the size is less than 1000, the number will be hidden and 0 will be returned due to privacy reasons. Otherwise, the number will be rounded off to two significant digits. Only applicable to first party audiences. Only returned in GET request.
---@field gmailAudienceSize? string Output only. The estimated audience size for Gmail network. If the size is less than 1000, the number will be hidden and 0 will be returned due to privacy reasons. Otherwise, the number will be rounded off to two significant digits. Only applicable to first party audiences. Only returned in GET request.
---@field displayName? string Optional. The display name of the first party and partner audience.
---@field firstPartyAndPartnerAudienceId? string Identifier. The unique ID of the first party and partner audience. Assigned by the system.
---@field membershipDurationDays? string Optional. The duration in days that an entry remains in the audience after the qualifying event. The set value must be greater than 0 and less than or equal to 540. Only applicable to first party audiences. This field is required if one of the following audience_type is used: * `CUSTOMER_MATCH_CONTACT_INFO` * `CUSTOMER_MATCH_DEVICE_ID`
---@field firstPartyAndPartnerAudienceType? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.FirstPartyAndPartnerAudienceFirstPartyAndPartnerAudienceTypeEnum|string Output only. Whether the audience is a first party and partner audience.
---@field description? string Optional. The user-provided description of the audience. Only applicable to first party audiences.
---@field mobileDeviceIdList? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.MobileDeviceIdList Input only. A list of mobile device IDs to define the initial audience members. Only applicable to audience_type `CUSTOMER_MATCH_DEVICE_ID`
---@field audienceType? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.FirstPartyAndPartnerAudienceAudienceTypeEnum|string Immutable. The type of the audience.
---@field contactInfoList? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.ContactInfoList Input only. A list of contact information to define the initial audience members. Only applicable to audience_type `CUSTOMER_MATCH_CONTACT_INFO`
---@field appId? string Optional. The app_id matches with the type of the mobile_device_ids being uploaded. Only applicable to audience_type `CUSTOMER_MATCH_DEVICE_ID`
---@field activeDisplayAudienceSize? string Output only. The estimated audience size for the Display network in the past month. If the size is less than 1000, the number will be hidden and 0 will be returned due to privacy reasons. Otherwise, the number will be rounded off to two significant digits. Only returned in GET request.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the first party and partner audience.
---@field advertiserId? string Required. The ID of the advertiser under whom the FirstPartyAndPartnerAudience will be created.

---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CreateGuaranteedOrdersRequest
---@field readWriteAdvertiserId? string The advertiser with read/write access to the guaranteed order. This is also the default advertiser of the guaranteed order.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.GuaranteedOrderStatus The status settings of the guaranteed order.
---@field defaultAdvertiserId? string Output only. The ID of default advertiser of the guaranteed order. The default advertiser is either the read_write_advertiser_id or, if that is not set, the first advertiser listed in read_advertiser_ids. Otherwise, there is no default advertiser.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the guaranteed order. Must be UTF-8 encoded with a maximum size of 240 bytes.
---@field legacyGuaranteedOrderId? string Output only. The legacy ID of the guaranteed order. Assigned by the original exchange. The legacy ID is unique within one exchange, but is not guaranteed to be unique across all guaranteed orders. This ID is used in SDF and UI.
---@field readAccessInherited? boolean Whether all advertisers of read_write_partner_id have read access to the guaranteed order. Only applicable if read_write_partner_id is set. If True, overrides read_advertiser_ids.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the guaranteed order.
---@field guaranteedOrderId? string Output only. The unique identifier of the guaranteed order. The guaranteed order IDs have the format `{exchange}-{legacy_guaranteed_order_id}`.
---@field publisherName? string Required. The publisher name of the guaranteed order. Must be UTF-8 encoded with a maximum size of 240 bytes.
---@field defaultCampaignId? string The ID of the default campaign that is assigned to the guaranteed order. The default campaign must belong to the default advertiser.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the guaranteed order was last updated. Assigned by the system.
---@field readWritePartnerId? string The partner with read/write access to the guaranteed order.
---@field readAdvertiserIds? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.StringList The IDs of advertisers with read access to the guaranteed order. This field must not include the advertiser assigned to read_write_advertiser_id if it is set. All advertisers in this field must belong to read_write_partner_id or the same partner as read_write_advertiser_id.
---@field exchange? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.GuaranteedOrderExchangeEnum|string Required. Immutable. The exchange where the guaranteed order originated.
---@field partnerId? string The ID of the partner that the request is being made within.
---@field advertiserId? string The ID of the advertiser that the request is being made within.

---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CreateInventorySourceGroupsAssignedInventorySourcesRequest
---@field assignedInventorySourceId? string Output only. The unique ID of the assigned inventory source. The ID is only unique within a given inventory source group. It may be reused in other contexts.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the assigned inventory source.
---@field inventorySourceId? string Required. The ID of the inventory source entity being targeted.
---@field inventorySourceGroupId string Required. The ID of the inventory source group to which the assignment will be assigned.
---@field partnerId? string The ID of the partner that owns the parent inventory source group. Only this partner will have write access to this assigned inventory source.
---@field advertiserId? string The ID of the advertiser that owns the parent inventory source group. The parent partner will not have access to this assigned inventory source.

---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CreateInventorySourceGroupsRequest
---@field inventorySourceGroupId? string Output only. The unique ID of the inventory source group. Assigned by the system.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the inventory source group.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the inventory source group. Must be UTF-8 encoded with a maximum size of 240 bytes.
---@field partnerId? string The ID of the partner that owns the inventory source group. Only this partner will have write access to this group. Only advertisers to which this group is explicitly shared will have read access to this group.
---@field advertiserId? string The ID of the advertiser that owns the inventory source group. The parent partner will not have access to this group.

---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CreateInventorySourcesRequest
---@field readAdvertiserIds? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.StringList Output only. The IDs of advertisers with read-only access to the inventory source.
---@field timeRange? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.TimeRange The time range when this inventory source starts and stops serving.
---@field commitment? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.InventorySourceCommitmentEnum|string Whether the inventory source has a guaranteed or non-guaranteed delivery.
---@field inventorySourceProductType? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.InventorySourceInventorySourceProductTypeEnum|string Output only. The product type of the inventory source, denoting the way through which it sells inventory.
---@field exchange? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.InventorySourceExchangeEnum|string The exchange to which the inventory source belongs.
---@field creativeConfigs? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CreativeConfigList The creative requirements of the inventory source. Not applicable for auction packages.
---@field displayName? string The display name of the inventory source. Must be UTF-8 encoded with a maximum size of 240 bytes.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.InventorySourceStatus The status settings of the inventory source.
---@field guaranteedOrderId? string Immutable. The ID of the guaranteed order that this inventory source belongs to. Only applicable when commitment is `INVENTORY_SOURCE_COMMITMENT_GUARANTEED`.
---@field publisherName? string The publisher/seller name of the inventory source.
---@field readWriteAccessors? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.InventorySourceAccessors The partner or advertisers that have read/write access to the inventory source. Output only when commitment is `INVENTORY_SOURCE_COMMITMENT_GUARANTEED`, in which case the read/write accessors are inherited from the parent guaranteed order. Required when commitment is `INVENTORY_SOURCE_COMMITMENT_NON_GUARANTEED`. If commitment is `INVENTORY_SOURCE_COMMITMENT_NON_GUARANTEED` and a partner is set in this field, all advertisers under this partner will automatically have read-only access to the inventory source. These advertisers will not be included in read_advertiser_ids.
---@field deliveryMethod? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.InventorySourceDeliveryMethodEnum|string The delivery method of the inventory source. * For non-guaranteed inventory sources, the only acceptable value is `INVENTORY_SOURCE_DELIVERY_METHOD_PROGRAMMATIC`. * For guaranteed inventory sources, acceptable values are `INVENTORY_SOURCE_DELIVERY_METHOD_TAG` and `INVENTORY_SOURCE_DELIVERY_METHOD_PROGRAMMATIC`.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the inventory source.
---@field inventorySourceType? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.InventorySourceInventorySourceTypeEnum|string Denotes the type of the inventory source.
---@field readPartnerIds? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.StringList Output only. The IDs of partners with read-only access to the inventory source. All advertisers of partners in this field inherit read-only access to the inventory source.
---@field dealId? string The ID in the exchange space that uniquely identifies the inventory source. Must be unique across buyers within each exchange but not necessarily unique across exchanges.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the inventory source was last updated. Assigned by the system.
---@field rateDetails? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.RateDetails Required. The rate details of the inventory source.
---@field inventorySourceId? string Output only. The unique ID of the inventory source. Assigned by the system.
---@field advertiserId? string The ID of the advertiser that the request is being made within.
---@field partnerId? string The ID of the partner that the request is being made within.

---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.CreatePartnersChannelsRequest
---@field negativelyTargetedLineItemCount? string Output only. Number of line items that are directly targeting this channel negatively.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the channel.
