---@alias gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.FloodlightActivityServingStatusEnum "FLOODLIGHT_ACTIVITY_SERVING_STATUS_UNSPECIFIED"|"FLOODLIGHT_ACTIVITY_SERVING_STATUS_ENABLED"|"FLOODLIGHT_ACTIVITY_SERVING_STATUS_DISABLED"

---A single Floodlight group.
---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.FloodlightGroup
---@field customVariables? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.DocumentMap User-defined custom variables owned by the Floodlight group. Use custom Floodlight variables to create reporting data that is tailored to your unique business needs. Custom Floodlight variables use the keys `U1=`, `U2=`, and so on, and can take any values that you choose to pass to them. You can use them to track virtually any type of data that you collect about your customers, such as the genre of movie that a customer purchases, the country to which the item is shipped, and so on. Custom Floodlight variables may not be used to pass any data that could be used or recognized as personally identifiable information (PII). Example: `custom_variables { fields { "U1": value { number_value: 123.4 }, "U2": value { string_value: "MyVariable2" }, "U3": value { string_value: "MyVariable3" } } }` Acceptable values for keys are "U1" through "U100", inclusive. String values must be less than 64 characters long, and cannot contain the following characters: `"<>`.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the Floodlight group.
---@field lookbackWindow? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.LookbackWindow Required. The lookback window for the Floodlight group. Both click_days and impression_days are required. Acceptable values for both are `0` to `90`, inclusive.
---@field webTagType? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.FloodlightGroupWebTagTypeEnum Required. The web tag type enabled for the Floodlight group.
---@field floodlightGroupId? string Output only. The unique ID of the Floodlight group. Assigned by the system.
---@field activeViewConfig? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.ActiveViewVideoViewabilityMetricConfig The Active View video viewability metric configuration for the Floodlight group.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the Floodlight group.

---@alias gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.FloodlightGroupWebTagTypeEnum "WEB_TAG_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"WEB_TAG_TYPE_NONE"|"WEB_TAG_TYPE_IMAGE"|"WEB_TAG_TYPE_DYNAMIC"

---Settings that control the number of times a user may be shown with the same ad during a given time period.
---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.FrequencyCap
---@field maxViews? number Optional. The maximum number of times a user may click-through or fully view an ad during this period until it is no longer served to them. Must be greater than 0. Only applicable to YouTube and Partners resources. Required when unlimited is `false` and max_impressions is not set.
---@field timeUnit? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.FrequencyCapTimeUnitEnum|string The time unit in which the frequency cap will be applied. Required when unlimited is `false`.
---@field timeUnitCount? number The number of time_unit the frequency cap will last. Required when unlimited is `false`. The following restrictions apply based on the value of time_unit: * `TIME_UNIT_MONTHS` - must be 1 * `TIME_UNIT_WEEKS` - must be between 1 and 4 * `TIME_UNIT_DAYS` - must be between 1 and 6 * `TIME_UNIT_HOURS` - must be between 1 and 23 * `TIME_UNIT_MINUTES` - must be between 1 and 59
---@field maxImpressions? number The maximum number of times a user may be shown the same ad during this period. Must be greater than 0. Required when unlimited is `false` and max_views is not set.
---@field unlimited? boolean Whether unlimited frequency capping is applied. When this field is set to `true`, the remaining frequency cap fields are not applicable.

---@alias gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v4.FrequencyCapTimeUnitEnum "TIME_UNIT_UNSPECIFIED"|"TIME_UNIT_LIFETIME"|"TIME_UNIT_MONTHS"|"TIME_UNIT_WEEKS"|"TIME_UNIT_DAYS"|"TIME_UNIT_HOURS"|"TIME_UNIT_MINUTES"

